{"3703440": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Actuator : Overt Abnormality", "steam_appid": 3703440, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "controller_support": "full", "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >&quot;Actuator : Overt Abnormality&quot; is a new kind of action RPG where leveling up expands your field of view.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Story</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >-This is a tale from not so long ago-</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The protagonist, searching for a rare battery, arrives in a certain district...</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The district seems strange somehow: there is no sign of people, and savage creatures roam there.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Relying on her natural athleticism, the protagonist faces the anomaly alone. (And goes looking for the battery, too.)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Action</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Straddle Vault</strong></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Because the protagonist is so athletic, she can vault over places a little taller than herself.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3703440/extras/44ba72a3140e19fc9fff26d100f0b47d.poster.avif?t=1778731267\" width=720 height=486 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3703440/extras/44ba72a3140e19fc9fff26d100f0b47d.webm?t=1778731267\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3703440/extras/44ba72a3140e19fc9fff26d100f0b47d.mp4?t=1778731267\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Actuator</strong></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The flashlight the protagonist carries can, if the conditions are right, move any &quot;object&quot; freely from a distance.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3703440/extras/5156a89d7e76bb19e962f0ee3ab57414.poster.avif?t=1778731267\" width=720 height=486 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3703440/extras/5156a89d7e76bb19e962f0ee3ab57414.webm?t=1778731267\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3703440/extras/5156a89d7e76bb19e962f0ee3ab57414.mp4?t=1778731267\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Player Level</strong></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Defeating enemies grants experience, and once that experience passes a certain amount, your Player Level rises.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >When your Player Level rises, your field of view becomes wider, letting you see more of the world. For example, you can read enemy attack patterns and dodge them, or spot hidden buildings more easily.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >(If you raise your level too much, you might start struggling to defeat smaller enemies...)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3703440/extras/a7074194c9ce375fcf94295e541e9090.poster.avif?t=1778731267\" width=720 height=486 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3703440/extras/a7074194c9ce375fcf94295e541e9090.webm?t=1778731267\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3703440/extras/a7074194c9ce375fcf94295e541e9090.mp4?t=1778731267\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >&quot;Actuator : Overt Abnormality&quot; is a new kind of action RPG where leveling up expands your field of view.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Story</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >-This is a tale from not so long ago-</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The protagonist, searching for a rare battery, arrives in a certain district...</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The district seems strange somehow: there is no sign of people, and savage creatures roam there.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Relying on her natural athleticism, the protagonist faces the anomaly alone. (And goes looking for the battery, too.)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Action</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Straddle Vault</strong></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Because the protagonist is so athletic, she can vault over places a little taller than herself.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3703440/extras/44ba72a3140e19fc9fff26d100f0b47d.poster.avif?t=1778731267\" width=720 height=486 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3703440/extras/44ba72a3140e19fc9fff26d100f0b47d.webm?t=1778731267\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3703440/extras/44ba72a3140e19fc9fff26d100f0b47d.mp4?t=1778731267\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Actuator</strong></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The flashlight the protagonist carries can, if the conditions are right, move any &quot;object&quot; freely from a distance.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3703440/extras/5156a89d7e76bb19e962f0ee3ab57414.poster.avif?t=1778731267\" width=720 height=486 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3703440/extras/5156a89d7e76bb19e962f0ee3ab57414.webm?t=1778731267\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3703440/extras/5156a89d7e76bb19e962f0ee3ab57414.mp4?t=1778731267\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Player Level</strong></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Defeating enemies grants experience, and once that experience passes a certain amount, your Player Level rises.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >When your Player Level rises, your field of view becomes wider, letting you see more of the world. For example, you can read enemy attack patterns and dodge them, or spot hidden buildings more easily.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >(If you raise your level too much, you might start struggling to defeat smaller enemies...)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3703440/extras/a7074194c9ce375fcf94295e541e9090.poster.avif?t=1778731267\" width=720 height=486 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3703440/extras/a7074194c9ce375fcf94295e541e9090.webm?t=177873126